# ============================================================================
# Generated files.
#
# Everything listed here is reproducible from source with `make` (see
# main/Makefile) and does not belong in the repository. `make clear` removes
# the same set locally.
#
# Note: .gitignore comments must be on their own line -- a trailing '#' is
# taken as part of the pattern, not as a comment.
# ============================================================================

## Core LaTeX auxiliary files
*.aux
*.log
*.toc
*.fot
*.fmt

# hyperref bookmarks
*.out
# hyperref backref
*.brf

# \listoffigures / \listoftables
*.lof
*.lot

## Intermediate documents
*.dvi
*.xdv
# graphicx, when it converts an included image
*-converted-to.*

## Bibliography: biblatex with the biber backend
*.bbl
*.bcf
*.blg
*.run.xml
*-blx.aux
*-blx.bib

# Left behind when a biber run aborts on a truncated .bcf. latexmk does not
# clean these up itself; `make clear` removes them explicitly.
*.bbl-SAVE-ERROR
*.bcf-SAVE-ERROR

## latexmk
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
latex.out/

## Editor <-> PDF source correlation
*.synctex
*.synctex.gz
*.synctex(busy)
*.synctex.gz(busy)
*.pdfsync
main/thesis.pdf

## Packages loaded in thesis.tex
# todonotes, via \listoftodos
*.tdo
# listings, via \lstlistoflistings
*.lol
# algorithm, via \listofalgorithms
*.loa
# theorem environments
*.thm
# xcolor
*.xcp

## Likely once figures are generated
# TikZ / PGF externalization
*.auxlock
*.md5
*.dpth
# gnuplot output from pgfplots
*.gnuplot
*.table

## Index and glossary, if ever used
*.idx
*.ilg
*.ind
*.glg
*.glo
*.gls
*.glsdefs
*.acn
*.acr
*.nlo
*.nls

## Editor and OS noise
*~
*.bak
*.bak[0-9]*
*.sav
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# AUCTeX
auto/
.texpadtmp/

# ============================================================================
# The built PDF is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# main/thesis.pdf is currently tracked, which keeps a readable copy of the
# thesis available straight from the repository -- convenient for handing to a
# supervisor without a local TeX installation. Uncomment the rule below to stop
# tracking it (and see the README/commit message for `git rm --cached`).
#
# Do NOT add a blanket `*.pdf` rule: \graphicspath points at figures/, so
# vector figures will be committed as PDFs and a blanket rule would silently
# exclude them. Ignore the build output by name instead.
#
# main/thesis.pdf
# ============================================================================
